andorra is a landlocked nation situated  right between spain and france  whom as you'll know both have a history  of expansion and conquering whatever  wasn't nailed down  despite its expansionist neighbours  andorra has managed to exist for over  750 years  which raises the question why why does  andorra exist  so to grossly oversimplify as of the  12th century the lands that made up  pandora were controlled by the church  and under the jurisdiction of the bishop  of virgil  now the church struggled to defend its  land and so the bishop of herzl turned  to the lords of cabo  to do the defending for them an  agreement was reached in that the lords  of cabo would be given the rights to tax  and conscript men in the region whereas  the church would retain ownership of  them these feudal rights soon went to  the council foie which is here and they  in the church had a good working  relationship  for about 50 years which was when the  sitting counterfoil started to pinch a  bunch of land from the church and  incorporated it into foie proper there  was some squabbling and with the  intervention of the king of aragon the  two sides came to an agreement the count  of foie would return the land that he  took and in return the church wouldn't  excommunicate him  also both the counterfoir and the bishop  of urgel would from then on rule andorra  as co-princes  this arrangement had little change until  1479.  this was when the count of four francis  phoebus inherited the kingdom of navarre  on top of his other lands  and less than a century later king henry  iii of navarre became king henry iv for  france and thus from then on one of the  co-princes of andorra was also the ruler  of france  and this is one of those things that  actually helped to secure andorra  it was now under the protection of  france and king louis xiii soon after  incorporated into the remaining kingdom  of navarre the spanish didn't mind  andorra being moved closer to france  because they themselves had several  reasons not to want it  the first was that economically andorra  had very little to offer and second the  people there were sympathetic to the  catalonians during their rebellions  against spain and so from the spanish  king's perspective andorra's inclusion  would do little but making catalonia  larger  and third it didn't want to annoy the  church as you'll know the french  monarchy would eventually go through  some difficult  times and when the french revolution was  well underway french leaders opted to  leave  andorra to its own devices so now  andorra was on its own  it did not like this turn of events and  so when napoleon was crowned the emperor  of france the andorrans asked for him to  return as their co-prince which he  accepted and then three years later  annexed catalonia and incorporated  andorra into it  napoleon was soon defeated and andorra  went back to being co-ruled by the  french king  and after france was finally done with  monarchy the french president  this status yet again put antora under  the protection of france which is why  when the spanish civil war broke out it  was stationed by french troops to  protect it  when world war ii broke out andorra  declared itself to be neutral  which technically wasn't true since it  had previously declared war against  germany in the last world war and wasn't  invited to the treaty of versailles and  so never technically made peace  but even when vichy france was dissolved  and occupied germany didn't move into  andorra and in effect it remained  neutral  and after france was liberated the last  threat to andorra was gone and its  position as an independent nation were  secured thereafter  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bissonette marvin cassell rob  waterhouse mo  james castaneda aaron the whites jordan  longley gustav swan  jerry lamdin marcus asner rasheed ali  miss izek coppertone spinning three  plates maggie paxkowsk